hadiths[224]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5155","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There are two blessings in which many people incur loss: health and free time.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5156","Al-Mustawrid bin Shaddad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: \By Allah! The example of this world in comparison to the Hereafter is just like one of you dipping his finger into the sea"","" then he should see how much (water) it returns with.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5157","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a dead goat with small ears and said: \Who among you would like to have this for one dirham?\"" The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said: \""We would not like to have it for anything insignificant.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""By Allah! The world is more insignificant in the sight of Allah than this (dead goat) is in your sight.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5158","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5159","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Allah does not waste any good deed of a believer; he is rewarded for it in this world and will be recompensed for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever"","" he is given provision in this world for the good deeds he did for Allah"","" until when he reaches the Hereafter"","" he will have no good deed left for which he may be rewarded.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5160","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Hell has been veiled with desires"","" and Paradise has been veiled with unpleasant things.\"" (Bukhari"","" Muslim). However"","" in Sahih Muslim"","" the word ((Hujibat)) is replaced with ((Huffat)). Agreed upon."""""
"5161","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Wretched is the slave of the dinar"","" the dirham"","" and the shawl; if he is given"","" he is pleased"","" and if he is not given"","" he is displeased. He is ruined and disgraced; if he is pricked by a thorn"","" may it not be removed. Glad tidings to that person who holds the reins of his horse in the way of Allah"","" his hair disheveled and his feet dusty; if he is appointed to guard duty"","" he remains steadfast in his post"","" and if he is in the rear of the army"","" he remains steadfast there as well. If he seeks permission (to attend a gathering)"","" he is not granted permission"","" and if he intercedes"","" his intercession is not accepted.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5162","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \What I fear most for you after me is that the doors of the splendor and adornment of the world will be opened for you.\"" A man asked: \""O Messenger of Allah! Will good bring evil with it?\"" The Prophet remained silent until we thought that revelation was being sent down to him. The narrator says"","" then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped the sweat from his (blessed face) and said: \""Where is the questioner?\"" As if he praised him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Good does not bring evil with it. Indeed"","" the spring season brings forth herbage"","" but some of it kills the animal"","" causes it to bloat"","" or brings it close to destruction. However"","" the animal that eats green grass eats until its flanks are filled"","" then it turns towards the sun"","" chews the cud"","" defecates and urinates"","" and then goes back and eats again. This wealth is lush and sweet; whoever takes it according to his need and spends it in its due right"","" it is the best helper. But whoever acquires it without need is like the one who eats but is never satisfied"","" and that (wealth) will testify against him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5163","Amr bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \By Allah! I do not fear poverty for you"","" but I fear that the world will be expanded for you as it was expanded for those before you"","" then you will compete for it as they competed for it"","" and it will destroy you as it destroyed them.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5164","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated: \O Allah! Provide for the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) only as much sustenance as will suffice to maintain the bond between their bodies and souls.\"" Agreed upon. In another narration it is stated: \""As much as is sufficient for subsistence\"" (grant livelihood enough for subsistence)."""""
"5165","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \He has succeeded who obeyed (his Lord)"","" was given provision sufficient for his needs"","" and was content with what Allah gave him.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5166","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \A servant says"","" 'My wealth"","" my wealth"",""' whereas his wealth is only in three ways: what he has consumed and finished"","" or worn and worn out"","" or given (in the way of Allah) and stored up (as reward). And whatever is besides these"","" he is leaving it behind for the people.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5167","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Three things accompany the deceased"","" two of them return and one remains with him: his family"","" his wealth"","" and his deeds go with him; his family and his wealth return"","" and his deeds remain with him.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5168","Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Who among you prefers the wealth of his heirs over his own wealth?\"" The companions replied: Each of us prefers his own wealth over the wealth of his heirs. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Indeed"","" his wealth is only that which he has sent forward"","" while the wealth he leaves behind is for his heirs.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5169","Mutarrif narrates from his father, who said: I presented myself before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reciting Surah At-Takathur. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The son of Adam says: 'My wealth"","" my wealth.' O son of Adam! Your wealth is only that which you have eaten and consumed"","" or worn and worn out"","" or given in charity and sent ahead (for the Hereafter).\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5170","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Wealth is not in the abundance of possessions and goods"","" rather true wealth is the richness of the soul (i.e."","" contentment).\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5171","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Who is there who will learn these words from me and act upon them"","" or teach them to someone who will act upon them?\"" I said: O Messenger of Allah! I will. So he took my hand and counted five things. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Avoid the prohibitions (things made unlawful by Allah)"","" and you will become the most devout worshipper among the people. Be content with what Allah has decreed for you"","" and you will become the richest of people. Treat your neighbor well"","" and you will be a believer. Love for people what you love for yourself"","" and you will be a Muslim. Do not laugh excessively"","" for excessive laughter deadens the heart.\"" Ahmad"","" Tirmidhi"","" and Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."""""
"5172","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" Allah says: O son of Adam! Free yourself for My worship"","" I will fill your heart with richness (contentment)"","" and I will remove your poverty. But if you do not do so"","" I will keep you busy with work and will not remove your poverty.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and Ibn Majah."""""
"5173","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The worship and intense devotion of a man was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the piety and caution of another man was also mentioned. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not compare (that worship and striving) with piety.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5174","Amr bin Maymun al-Awdi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) advised a man, saying: \Take advantage of five things before five: your youth before your old age"","" your health before your illness"","" your wealth before your poverty"","" your free time before your preoccupation"","" and your life before your death.\"" Imam Tirmidhi narrated it as a mursal hadith. Hasan"","" narrated by Tirmidhi."""""
"5175","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Does any one of you await overwhelming wealth"","" or poverty that makes one forget (obedience and worship)"","" or a disease that ruins"","" or old age that brings senseless talk"","" or sudden death"","" or the Dajjal—for the Dajjal is the worst awaited hidden trial—or the Hour"","" and the Hour is the greatest calamity and the most bitter thing.\"" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i."""""
"5176","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Behold! The world and whatever is in it are all accursed"","" except for the remembrance of Allah"","" the deeds beloved to Allah"","" and the scholar and the learner.\"" Its chain is good. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."""""
"5177","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “If the world (in importance) was worth even the wing of a mosquito in the sight of Allah, He would not have given a disbeliever even a sip of water from it.” Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad, al-Tirmidhi, and Ibn Majah."
"5178","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not establish estates"","" otherwise you will become engrossed in the world.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Tirmidhi and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5179","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever prefers the world has harmed his Hereafter"","" and whoever prefers the Hereafter has harmed his world. So give preference to that which is everlasting over that which is perishable.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5180","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \Cursed is the slave of the dirham and dinar.\"" Its chain is weak; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5181","Ka'b bin Malik narrates from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Two hungry wolves left among a flock of sheep do not cause as much harm to them as a man's greed for wealth and status does to his religion.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi and al-Darimi."""""
"5182","Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whatever a believer spends"","" he is rewarded for it"","" except for what he spends on this soil (beyond necessity)"","" for which he is not rewarded.\"" Sahih"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5183","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \All spending in the way of Allah is rewarded except for construction; there is no good in spending on it.\"" (Tirmidhi)"","" and he said this hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5184","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out one day and we were with him. He saw a tall dome and said: \What is this?\"" His companions replied"","" \""It belongs to an Ansari man.\"" The Prophet remained silent and kept it in his heart until its owner came and greeted the Prophet in the presence of the people"","" but the Prophet turned away from him. He did this several times until the man recognized the Prophet’s displeasure and estrangement towards him. He asked his companions about the reason and said"","" \""By Allah! I feel that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) is angry with me"","" but I do not know the reason.\"" They told him"","" \""You came out and saw your dome.\"" The man went to his dome"","" demolished it"","" and leveled it with the ground. Then one day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out and did not see the dome. He asked"","" \""What happened to the dome?\"" The companions replied"","" \""Its owner asked us the reason for your estrangement"","" so we told him"","" and he demolished it.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Listen! Every building which is not essential is a burden for its owner.\"" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Abu Dawood."""""
"5185","Abu Hashim bin Utbah narrates, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, advised me: \It is sufficient for you to accumulate only so much wealth that you have one servant and one mount for striving in the way of Allah.\"" Ahmad"","" Tirmidhi"","" Nasa'i"","" Ibn Majah"","" and in some copies of Mishkat"","" it is mentioned as Abu Hashim bin Utbad"","" i.e."","" with a dal instead of a ta"","" and this is a scribal error. Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ahmad"","" Tirmidhi"","" Nasa'i"","" Ibn Majah"","" and Mishkat al-Sunnah."""""
"5186","It is narrated from Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A person has no right to anything except these three things: a house for residence"","" clothing to cover his nakedness"","" and bread and water.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Tirmidhi."""""
"5187","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Tell me of an action which, if I do it, Allah and people will love me.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Renounce the world and Allah will love you, and renounce what people possess and people will love you.” Weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."
"5188","It is narrated from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slept on a mat, and when he got up, the marks of that (mat) were visible on his blessed body. Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \O Messenger of Allah! If you command us"","" we will prepare a soft bed for you.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""What have I to do with the world? I and the world are like a rider who stops under the shade of a tree"","" then departs and leaves it behind.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Ahmad"","" al-Tirmidhi"","" and Ibn Majah."""""
"5189","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: \Among my friends"","" the believer who is most enviable to me is the one who has little worldly possessions"","" finds delight in prayer"","" worships his Lord excellently"","" obeys Him even in private"","" is not well-known among people"","" fingers do not point towards him"","" his sustenance is just sufficient"","" and he is patient over it.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) snapped his fingers and said: \""His death comes quickly"","" his mourners are few"","" and his inheritance is little.\"" Its chain is weak; narrated by Ahmad"","" al-Tirmidhi"","" and Ibn Majah."""""
"5190","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \My Lord offered me to turn the valley of Batha in Makkah (or the pebbles of Makkah) into gold for me. I said: 'My Lord! No"","" rather I wish that I may be satiated one day and hungry another day. When I am hungry"","" I humble myself before You and remember You"","" and when I am satiated"","" I praise You and give thanks to You.'\"" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Ahmad and al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5191","Ubaydullah bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever among you wakes up in the morning feeling secure with regard to his family"","" healthy in his body"","" and possessing food for one day"","" it is as if the whole world has been gathered for him from all sides.\"" (Tirmidhi)"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5192","Miqdam bin Ma’dikarib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “No man fills a vessel worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for a person to eat a few mouthfuls to keep his back straight. But if he must (eat more), then one third (of his stomach) should be for food, one third for drink, and one third for air.” Sahih, narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."
"5193","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard a man belching, so he said: \Reduce your belching"","" for on the Day of Resurrection"","" the person who used to eat to his fill in the world will remain hungry for a long time among the people.\"" Sharh al-Sunnah"","" and Imam Tirmidhi has narrated it in the same way. Weak"","" narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah and Tirmidhi."""""
"5194","Ka'b bin 'Iyad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: \Every nation has had a trial (test and tribulation)"","" and the trial of my nation is wealth.\"" Its chain is authentic"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5195","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: \On the Day of Resurrection"","" a person will be presented like a goat's kid (in humiliation)"","" and he will be made to stand before Allah. Allah will say to him: I granted you (life and senses"","" health and well-being)"","" I gave you servants and attendants"","" and (by sending prophets and books) I bestowed favors upon you"","" so what did you do? He will say: O my Lord! I accumulated (wealth)"","" increased it"","" and left behind more than what I had"","" so send me back and I will bring it all to You. He will be told: Show Me what you sent ahead. Then he will say the same again: I accumulated it"","" increased it"","" and left behind more than what I had"","" so send me back and I will bring it all to You. Thus"","" he will be such a (wretched) person who did not send forth any good deeds"","" and he will be sent towards Hell.\"" (Tirmidhi"","" and he declared it weak. Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Tirmidhi.)"""""
"5196","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \On the Day of Resurrection"","" the first question that will be asked of a servant regarding blessings will be: Did We not make your body healthy"","" and (did) We not quench your thirst with cool water?\"" Its chain is authentic"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5197","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: \On the Day of Resurrection"","" the feet of a person will not move (from the court of Allah) until he is questioned about five things: about his life—how he spent it; about his youth—where he wasted it; about his wealth—how he earned it and where he spent it; and about how much he acted upon the knowledge he had.\"" Tirmidhi"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5198","It is narrated from Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \You are not better than a red-skinned person nor a black-skinned person"","" except that you excel him through piety.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5199","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a servant adopts indifference towards the world"","" Allah creates wisdom in his heart"","" causes it to flow from his tongue"","" grants him insight into the faults of the world"","" its ailments"","" and their remedies"","" and leads him safely from it towards the Abode of Peace (Paradise).\"" Its chain of narration is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5200","It is narrated from Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Successful is the one whose heart Allah has made pure for faith"","" whose heart He has kept safe (from envy"","" malice"","" etc.)"","" whose tongue He has made truthful"","" whose soul He has made content"","" whose nature He has made upright"","" whose ears He has made attentive to (the truth)"","" and whose eyes He has made observant (of evidence). The ears are funnels for what the heart preserves"","" and the eyes are the place of settlement and stability. And successful is the one who has made his heart a guardian.\"" Its chain is weak; narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5201","Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When you see Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" giving the world to a servant despite his disobedience (the disobedience) which He does not like"","" then it is a plan (from Allah).\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: \""So when they forgot that by which they had been reminded"","" We opened to them the doors of everything"","" until when they rejoiced in that which they were given"","" We seized them suddenly"","" and they were then plunged into destruction and despair.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5202","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man from among the people of Suffah passed away and he left behind one dinar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(This dinar) is a mark (of blame).” The narrator states, then another man passed away and he left behind two dinars, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(These two dinars) are two marks (of blame).” Sahih, narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"5203","It is narrated from Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he went to visit his maternal uncle Abu Hashim bin Utbah (may Allah be pleased with him) when Abu Hashim (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep. He asked, \Dear uncle! What is making you weep? Is it some pain that is troubling you"","" or is it greed for the world?\"" He replied"","" \""Not at all. Rather"","" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) advised us"","" but I did not act upon it.\"" He asked"","" \""What was that (advice)?\"" He said"","" \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'It is sufficient for you to accumulate only so much wealth that you have a servant and a mount for striving in the way of Allah.' And I think that I have accumulated (more wealth than that).\"" Weak"","" narrated by Ahmad"","" al-Tirmidhi"","" al-Nasa'i"","" and Ibn Majah."""""
"5204","Umm Darda (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I said to Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him): Why is it that you do not seek (wealth and status) like so-and-so? He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: \Ahead of you is a difficult pass which those carrying heavy loads will not be able to cross.\"" I wish to keep my load light for passing through that pass. Its chain of narration is weak; it is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5205","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Is there anyone who walks on water but his feet do not get wet?\"" They replied"","" \""O Messenger of Allah! No.\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""A worldly person is like this; he cannot remain safe from sins.\"" Both these hadiths have been narrated by Imam Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5206","Jubair bin Nufair (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates in a mursal tradition, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \It has not been revealed to me that I should accumulate wealth and become one of the traders"","" rather it has been revealed to me that: 'Glorify your Lord with His praise and be among those who prostrate"","" and worship your Lord until death comes to you.'\"" Sharh al-Sunnah"","" and Abu Nu'aim narrated from Abu Muslim in al-Hilyah. Its chain is weak. Narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah and in Hilyat al-Awliya."""""
"5207","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever seeks the world in a lawful manner"","" to avoid begging"","" to spend on his family"","" and to show kindness to his neighbor"","" then on the Day of Resurrection he will meet Allah Almighty with his face shining like the full moon of the fourteenth night. And whoever seeks the world in a lawful manner to increase his wealth"","" to boast to others"","" and for show-off"","" then he will meet Allah Almighty in such a state that He will be angry with him.\"" Its chain is weak; narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5208","It is narrated from Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Indeed, there are treasures of goodness, and there are keys to these treasures. Glad tidings for the servant whom Allah has made a key (opener) for goodness and a lock for evil, and destruction for the servant whom Allah has made an opener for evil and a lock for goodness.” Its chain is very weak. Narrated by Ibn Majah."
"5209","Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \When there is no blessing placed in a servant's wealth"","" he spends that wealth on water and clay (i.e."","" construction).\"" Its chain of narration is weak. It is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5210","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Beware of (committing) the unlawful in matters of construction"","" for it is the foundation of ruin.\"" Both narrations have been reported by Imam Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5211","Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \The world is the home of the one who has no home"","" the wealth of the one who has no wealth"","" and only the one who is not wise gathers it (the world).\"" Its chain is weak; narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5212","Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying during a sermon: \Wine is the sum of all sins"","" women are the snares of Satan"","" and the love of the world is the root and foundation of every sin.\"" The narrator states: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: \""Keep women behind as Allah has kept them behind.\"" I did not find it; narrated by Razeen."""""
"5213","And Imam Bayhaqi narrated it as mursal with a hasan chain in Shu'ab al-Iman: \Love of the world is the root of all sins.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5214","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \What I fear most for my Ummah is the desires of the self and prolonged hopes"","" for the desires of the self prevent from the truth"","" while prolonged hopes make one forget the Hereafter. And this world is (imperceptibly) departing"","" while the Hereafter is (similarly) approaching"","" and each of them has seekers. Do not be seekers of this world; keep performing deeds"","" for today you are in the abode of action and there is no reckoning"","" and tomorrow you will be in the abode of the Hereafter and there will be no action.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5215","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The world is passing away while the Hereafter is coming, and each of them has seekers. You should be seekers of the Hereafter and not seekers of the world, because today is the time for action and not for reckoning, while tomorrow will be for reckoning and not for action. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5216","It is narrated from Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon one day, and in his sermon he said: \Listen! The world is a present wealth; both the righteous and the wicked eat from it. Listen! The Hereafter is an inevitable reality; at that time"","" the All-Powerful King will judge between the righteous and the wicked. Listen! All good is completely in Paradise"","" and listen! All evil is completely in Hell. And listen! Keep performing deeds"","" fear Allah (from the fear of evil occurring)"","" and know that you will be presented with your deeds. Whoever has done an atom's weight of good will see it"","" and whoever has done an atom's weight of evil will also see it.\"" Imam Shafi'i has narrated this. Its chain is very weak. Narrated by al-Shafi'i."""""
"5217","Shaddad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \O people! Indeed"","" the world is present wealth; every righteous and wicked person eats from it. The Hereafter is a certain reality and a true promise. The Just"","" All-Powerful King will judge on that Day; He will establish the truth therein and eradicate falsehood. Be seekers of the Hereafter"","" not seekers of the world. Indeed"","" every child follows its mother.\"" Its chain is weak. Abu Nu'aym narrated it in Hilyat al-Awliya."""""
"5218","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When the sun rises"","" two angels call out from its two edges"","" making all creatures except jinn and humans hear their voices: O people! Come to your Lord. That (wealth) which is little but sufficient is better than that which is abundant but distracts (from the remembrance of Allah).\"" Both ahadith have been narrated by Abu Nu'aym in Al-Hilya. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Abu Nu'aym in Hilyat al-Awliya."""""
"5219","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in a marfu‘ (attributed to the Prophet) tradition: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \When a person dies"","" the angels say: 'What has he sent forward (of deeds)?' And people say: 'What has he left behind (of wealth)?'\"" Its chain is weak. It is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu‘ab al-Iman."""""
"5220","It is narrated from Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) that Luqman said to his son: \My son! Indeed"","" that which has been promised to people has become prolonged for them"","" and they are swiftly heading towards the Hereafter. And ever since you have come into this world"","" you have been (gradually) leaving it behind and advancing towards the Hereafter. Indeed"","" the home towards which you are journeying is closer to you than the home from which you have set out.\"" I did not find it"","" narrated by Razeen."""""
"5221","Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: It was asked to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), \Which person is the best?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""Every person with a pure heart and a truthful tongue.\"" The companions said"","" \""We know about a truthful tongue"","" but what is meant by a pure heart?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""It is the pure and clean heart in which there is neither sin"","" nor injustice"","" nor malice"","" nor envy.\"" Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Ibn Majah and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5222","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There are four things"","" if they are found in you"","" then even if you do not attain the world"","" there is no harm or deficiency: safeguarding trust"","" truthfulness in speech"","" good character"","" and abstaining from unlawful food.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5223","It is narrated from Imam Malik, he said: I have received the hadith that Luqman the Wise was asked, \By which things have you reached the position in which we see you?\"" He replied: Truthfulness"","" fulfilling trusts"","" and leaving aside useless things. Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Malik."""""
"5224","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Deeds will come (to intercede before Allah)"","" prayer will come and say"","" 'O Lord! I am prayer.' He will say"","" 'You are upon goodness.' Charity will come and say"","" 'O Lord! I am charity.' He will say"","" 'You are upon goodness.' Then fasting will come and say"","" 'O Lord! I am fasting.' He will say"","" 'You are upon goodness.' Then"","" in this manner"","" deeds will keep coming"","" and Allah"","" the Exalted"","" will keep saying"","" 'You are upon goodness.' Then Islam will come and say"","" 'O Lord! You are Peace and I am Islam.' Allah"","" the Exalted"","" will say"","" 'You are upon goodness. Today"","" because of you I will call to account and because of you I will grant.' Allah"","" the Exalted"","" has said in His Book: 'Whoever seeks a religion other than Islam"","" it will never be accepted from him"","" and he will be among the losers in the Hereafter.' Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ahmad.\"""""""
"5225","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We had a curtain with pictures of birds on it. (Upon seeing this) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Aisha! Change it"","" for when I see it"","" it reminds me of the world (I remember the world).\"" Sahih"","" narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5226","Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, \Give me a brief advice.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""When you pray"","" pray as if it is your farewell prayer. Do not say anything for which you would have to apologize tomorrow"","" and be completely hopeless and detached from what people possess.\"" Weak"","" narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5227","Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him to Yemen, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went out with him to advise him. At that time, Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) was riding, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was walking alongside his mount. When he finished, he said: “Mu’adh, it may be that you will not meet me after this year; perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave.” Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep out of fear of separation from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned his face towards Madinah and said: “The most deserving of my closeness and intercession are the God-fearing, whoever they may be and wherever they may be.” All four ahadith are narrated by Imam Ahmad. Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad."
"5228","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: \Allah opens the breast of the one whom He intends to guide to Islam.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""When light enters the breast"","" the breast opens up.\"" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Is there any sign by which it can be recognized? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Yes"","" distancing oneself from the house of deception (the world)"","" turning towards the eternal home (the Hereafter)"","" and preparing for death before death comes.\"" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5229","It is narrated from Abu Huraira and Abu Khallad, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When you see a servant who has been granted indifference towards the world and is of few words"","" then seek his company"","" for he has been granted wisdom.\"" Both narrations have been transmitted by Imam Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman. Weak"","" narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5230","It is narrated from Abu Huraira and Abu Khalad that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When you see a servant who has been given disinterest in the world and he is low-spirited"","" then draw close to him because he has been given wisdom.\"" Weak"","" Rawaah al-Bayhaqi fi Shub al-Iman."""""
"5231","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Many a person with disheveled hair"","" who is turned away from doors"","" if he swears by Allah"","" Allah fulfills it for him.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5232","Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrates that Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) thought that he had superiority and excellence over those who were of a lower status than him (in generosity). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \You are given help and provision only because of your weak ones.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5233","Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \On the night of Mi'raj"","" I stood at the gate of Paradise and saw that most of those entering it were the poor"","" while the wealthy were held back"","" and the people of the Fire (i.e."","" the disbelievers) had been ordered to Hell. And I stood at the gate of Hell and saw that the majority of those entering it were women.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5234","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I looked into Paradise and saw that the majority of its inhabitants were the poor"","" and I looked into Hell and saw that the majority of its inhabitants were women.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5235","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The poor among the emigrants will enter Paradise forty years before the wealthy on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5236","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to a person sitting with him: “What is your opinion about this (man)?” He replied: “He is one of the honorable people. By Allah! He is such that if he proposes marriage anywhere, he should be married, and if he intercedes, his intercession should be accepted.” The narrator says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. Then another man passed by, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “What is your opinion about this man?” He replied: “O Messenger of Allah! He is one of the poor Muslims. He is such that if he proposes marriage anywhere, he should not be married, and if he intercedes, his intercession should not be accepted, and if he speaks, his words should not be listened to.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “This (single) man is better than a whole earth full of people like the first one.” Agreed upon."
"5237","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The family of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not eat their fill of barley bread for two consecutive days until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away. Agreed upon."
"5238","Saeed Maqbari (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he passed by some people who had a roasted goat before them. They invited him (to eat), but he refused to eat it and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed from this world and he never ate his fill of barley bread. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5239","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he took barley bread and discolored fat to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) armor was mortgaged with a Jew in Madinah. He had taken barley from him for his family. And I (the narrator) heard Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: In the house of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there was not even a sa’ of wheat nor a sa’ of any other grain in the evening, while he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had nine pure wives. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5240","Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was lying on a mat made of date-palm leaves, and he had not spread any bedding or anything else. The marks of the mat were visible on his side, and he was leaning on a leather pillow stuffed with palm tree leaves. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah to grant abundance to your Ummah, for the Persians and Romans have been greatly favored, even though they do not worship Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \O Ibn Khattab! Are you still at that position? These (disbelievers) are people whose pleasures have been hastened for them in this worldly life.\"" In another narration"","" it is stated: \""Are you not pleased that for them is this world and for us is the Hereafter?\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5241","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I met seventy of the Companions of Suffah, and not a single one of them had a large cloak. Each of them either had a lower garment or a single sheet, and they had tied its edge around their necks. Some of those sheets reached halfway down their shins, and some reached their ankles, and they would gather it with their hands so that their private parts would not become uncovered. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5242","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When any one of you sees someone who is superior to him in wealth and appearance"","" then he should look at someone who is inferior to him.\"" And in the narration of Muslim"","" he said: \""(In worldly matters) look at someone who is below you and do not look at someone who is above you"","" for this is more appropriate so that you do not belittle the blessings of Allah which He has bestowed upon you.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5243","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The poor will enter Paradise five hundred years before the rich"","" which is half a day.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Tirmidhi."""""
"5244","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \O Allah! Keep me alive as a poor person"","" cause me to die as a poor person"","" and gather me among the group of the poor.\"" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) asked: O Messenger of Allah! Why? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Because they will enter Paradise forty years before the wealthy. Aisha! Do not turn away any poor person empty-handed"","" even if it is with a piece of a date. Aisha! Love the poor"","" keep them close to you"","" so that on the Day of Resurrection Allah will keep you close to Himself.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5245","And Ibn Majah narrated from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) up to \be raised among the group of the poor.\"" Its chain of narration is weak"","" narrated by Ibn Majah."""""
"5246","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: \Seek me among your weak ones"","" for you are given provision and help only because of your weak ones.\"" Sahih"","" narrated by Abu Dawood."""""
"5247","Umayyah bin Khalid bin Abdullah bin Asid narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he used to seek victory through the prayers of the poor emigrants. Its chain is weak, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"5248","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Do not envy a wicked person for the blessings he enjoys"","" for you do not know what will happen to him after his death. With Allah"","" there is a deadly thing for him that will never die.\"" That is: Hell. Its chain of narration is weak"","" narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."""""
"5249","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The world is a prison and a famine for the believer; when he departs from the world"","" he is separated from the prison and the famine.\"" Its chain is weak; it is narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."""""
"5250","It is narrated from Qatadah bin Nu’man (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When Allah loves a servant"","" He protects him from (the wealth and status of) the world just as one of you protects his sick one from water.\"" Sahih"","" narrated by Ahmad and al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5251","It is narrated from Mahmood bin Labeed (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There are two things which man dislikes: Man dislikes death"","" although death is better for the believer than tribulation"","" and he dislikes the scarcity of wealth"","" while the reckoning for little wealth is lighter.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5252","Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, \I love you.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""See what you are saying.\"" He said"","" \""By Allah! I love you.\"" He said this three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""If you are truthful (in your claim)"","" then prepare a shield to face poverty"","" for indeed"","" poverty comes to the one who loves me faster than a flood.\"" (Tirmidhi) And he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5253","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \No one has been frightened in the way of Allah as much as I have been frightened"","" and no one has been harmed in the way of Allah as much as I have been harmed. Thirty days and nights have passed over me and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) in such a state that there was nothing for us to eat that any living being could eat"","" except for a small amount that Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) could hide under his armpit.\"" And Imam Tirmidhi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The meaning of this hadith is that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) escaped from Makkah"","" Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was with him"","" and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) had only as much food as he could keep under his armpit. Its chain is authentic"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5254","Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We complained of hunger to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and we lifted our garments from our stomachs to show a stone tied to it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) then showed us two stones tied to his own stomach. __REF_N__ Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5255","It is narrated from Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that he felt hungry, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, gave him one date at a time. Its chain is authentic; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5256","Amr bin Shu'aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that they narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \There are two qualities; whoever possesses them"","" Allah writes him as grateful and patient. Whoever"","" in matters of religion"","" looks at someone above him and follows him"","" and in worldly matters looks at someone below him and thanks Allah for the superiority He has granted him over that person"","" then Allah writes him as grateful and patient. And whoever"","" in matters of religion"","" looks at someone below him and in worldly matters looks at someone above him and grieves over what he has not received"","" then Allah does not write him as grateful and patient.\"" Its chain is weak; it is narrated by al-Tirmidhi. And the hadith narrated from Abu Sa'id: \""Rejoice"","" O poor group of emigrants"",""\"" is mentioned after the chapter on the virtues of the Qur'an."""""
"5257","Abu Abdur Rahman Hubli narrates: I heard Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) say, a man asked him: Are we not among the poor emigrants? Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: Do you have a wife with whom you spend the night? He said: Yes! He said: Do you have a house to live in? He said: Yes! He said: Then you are among the wealthy. He said: I even have a servant. He said: Then you are a king. Abdur Rahman said: Three men came to Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him), and I was with him at that time. They said: Abu Muhammad! By Allah! We have nothing, no expenses, no ride, and no belongings. He said to them: What do you want? If you wish, you may come to us, and whatever Allah has made available to us, we will give to you. And if you wish, we can mention your case to the king. And if you wish, you may be patient, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \The poor emigrants will enter Paradise forty years before the wealthy on the Day of Resurrection.\"" They said: We will be patient and we will not ask for anything. Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5258","Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was sitting in the mosque while a group of the poor Muhajirun were also gathered in a circle. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived, he joined their circle, and I also got up and went towards them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Give glad tidings to the poor Muhajirun of that which will make their faces rejoice"","" for they will enter Paradise forty years before the wealthy.\"" The narrator states: I saw that their faces began to shine"","" and Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Until I wished that I was with them or among them. Sahih"","" narrated by Al-Darimi."""""
"5259","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: My beloved (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me regarding seven things. He (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me to love the poor and to remain close to them. He commanded me to look towards those who are lower than me (in worldly matters) and not to look towards those who are above me. He commanded me to maintain ties of kinship even if they cut me off. He commanded me not to ask anything from anyone. He commanded me to speak the truth even if it is bitter. He commanded me not to fear the blame of any blamer regarding Allah (the truth). And he commanded me to recite ((Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh)) frequently, for these words are among the treasures beneath the Throne. ‘‘ Its chain is Hasan, narrated by Ahmad."
"5260","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) liked three things of this world: food, women, and perfume. Two of these were granted to him and one was not. He was granted women (the pure wives, may Allah be pleased with them) and perfume, but (satisfying) food was not granted to him. Its chain is weak, narrated by Ahmad."
"5261","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Fragrance and women have been made beloved to me"","" and the coolness of my eyes is in prayer.\"" Ahmad"","" Nasa'i"","" and Ibn Jawzi have reported the addition of ((min al-dunya)) after ((hubbiba ilayya)). Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and Nasa'i."""""
"5262","It is narrated from Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen, he said: \Beware of living a life of luxury"","" for the (sincere) servants of Allah are not those who live in luxury.\"" Its chain is weak; narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5263","Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him and his family) said: \Whoever is content with the little provision given by Allah"","" Allah becomes pleased with his little deeds.\"" Its chain is weak; it was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5264","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever is afflicted with hunger or is in need of something and conceals it from people"","" it is a right upon Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" to grant him lawful sustenance for a year.\"" Both narrations have been transmitted by Imam Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman. Its chain of narration is very weak. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5265","Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" Allah loves His believing servant who has dependents and"","" despite being in need"","" does not ask (others).\"" Its chain is weak; narrated by Ibn Majah."""""
"5266","Zaid bin Aslam (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: One day Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked for water, and honey mixed with water was presented to him. He said: \This is very good"","" but I hear the command of Allah"","" the Exalted"","" that He criticized a people for their desires"","" saying: 'You have received your good things in the life of this world and you have enjoyed them.' I fear that the reward for our good deeds may be given to us in this world only.\"" Therefore"","" he did not drink it. Lam Ajidahu"","" narrated by Razeen."""""
"5267","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We had never eaten dates to our fill before the conquest of Khaybar. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5268","Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a square-shaped line and drew a line in the middle of it extending outside, and drew some small lines on the side of this middle line, and said: \This is man"","" and this is his appointed term (death) which surrounds him"","" and the one going outwards is his hope"","" and these small lines are the calamities that befall him. If one misses him"","" another seizes him"","" and if that one misses him"","" yet another seizes him.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5269","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew some lines and said: \This is hope"","" and this is his death. While he is in this state"","" the nearest line suddenly reaches him.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5270","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A person grows old"","" but two things in him remain young: the desire for wealth and the desire for a long life.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5271","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \The heart of an old person remains young in two things: in the love of the world and in long hopes.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5272","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Allah has removed the excuse of the person whose life He prolonged until He let him reach sixty years of age (for not repenting and not doing good deeds).\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5273","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \If a man had two valleys full of wealth"","" he would seek a third one. Nothing fills the belly of man except (the grave's) dust"","" and Allah accepts the repentance of the one who repents.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5274","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, took hold of a part of my body and said: \Live in this world as if you are a stranger or a traveler"","" and count yourself among the inhabitants of the graves (the dead).\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5275","Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while I and my mother were plastering a part of (our) house. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Abdullah! What is happening?\"" I replied"","" \""We are repairing a part (of the house).\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The matter (of death) is swifter than this.\"" Ahmad"","" Tirmidhi"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Sahih"","" narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."""""
"5276","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would urinate, he would perform tayammum with soil. I said, \O Messenger of Allah! Water is near you.\"" He"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" said: \""How do I know"","" perhaps I may not be able to reach there.\"" Sharh al-Sunnah"","" and Ibn al-Jawzi narrated it in the book \""Al-Wafa.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."""""
"5277","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \This is man and this is his death.\"" And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his hand at the back of his neck"","" then opened it and said: \""And there are his desires.\"" Its chain is authentic; narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5278","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed a stick in front of him, one at its side, and one at a distance. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do you know what this is?\"" The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""This is man"","" and this is his appointed time (death).\"" The narrator states: I think the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""These are his hopes; he strives to achieve his hopes"","" but before his hope is fulfilled"","" death overtakes him.\"" Its chain is Hasan. It is narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."""""
"5279","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The lifespan of my Ummah is between sixty and seventy years.\"" (Tirmidhi)"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is hasan"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5280","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The ages of my Ummah are between sixty and seventy years"","" and those who exceed this (sixty"","" seventy) are few among them.\"" Tirmidhi"","" Ibn Majah. Hasan"","" narrated by Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah. And the hadith narrated from Abdullah bin Shukhair has already been mentioned in the chapter on visiting the sick."""""
"5281","Amr bin Shu’aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The first righteousness of this Ummah is (firm) belief in the Hereafter and indifference towards the world, while its first corruption is miserliness and (unlimited) desires.” Its chain is weak; narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"5282","Sufyan Thawri (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \Wearing coarse"","" rough clothes and eating dry"","" simple food is not called renunciation of the world; rather"","" having fewer desires is renunciation of the world.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."""""
"5283","Zaid bin Hussain (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates, I heard from Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him), he was asked, what is meant by renunciation of the world? He replied: Lawful earning and having few hopes. Its chain of narration is weak, narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."
"5284","Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah loves the wealthy person who is pious and unknown.” Narrated by Muslim. And the hadith narrated from Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): “Envy is only (permissible) towards two persons” has already been mentioned in the chapter on the virtues of the Qur’an."
"5285","It is narrated from Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked, \O Messenger of Allah! Which person is the best?\"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: \""The one whose life is long and whose deeds are good (i.e."","" according to the Qur'an and Sunnah).\"" The man asked"","" \""Who is the worst person?\"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: \""The one whose life is long and whose deeds are bad.\"" Chain is weak"","" narrated by Ahmad and al-Darimi."""""
"5286","It is narrated from Ubayd bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between two men. One of them was martyred in the way of Allah, and then the other died about a week later. When the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) offered his funeral prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \What supplication did you make for him?\"" They replied"","" \""We prayed to Allah to forgive him"","" have mercy on him"","" and unite him with his companion.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Where did the prayers go that he offered after his companion's prayers? And where did the deeds go that he performed after him?\"" Or he said: \""Where did the fasts go that he observed after him?\"" The distance between the two is greater than the distance between the earth and the sky.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Abu Dawood and Nasa'i."""""
"5287","It is narrated from Abu Kabsha Anmari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: \There are three qualities upon which I swear"","" and I will tell you a hadith"","" so remember it. The things upon which I swear are these: Charity does not decrease a servant's wealth; if a servant is wronged and he is patient over it"","" then Allah increases his honor in return; and when a servant asks from others"","" Allah makes him fall into poverty. As for the thing I am going to tell you"","" remember it well.\"" Then he said: \""The world is for four kinds of people: One is the servant whom Allah has given wealth and knowledge"","" and he fears his Lord regarding it"","" maintains family ties"","" and acts for the sake of Allah according to that (knowledge); this is the highest rank. Another is the servant whom Allah has given knowledge but not wealth"","" and his intention is good; he says: If I had wealth"","" I would spend like such-and-such (wealthy) person; the reward for both of them is equal. And another is the servant whom Allah has given wealth but not knowledge"","" so he goes astray because of his wealth without knowledge"","" and he neither fears his Lord"","" nor maintains family ties"","" nor spends it as is right; this person is at the worst level. And another is the servant whom Allah has given neither wealth nor knowledge"","" and he says: If I had wealth"","" I would act (i.e."","" spend) like such-and-such person; he only intends (evil)"","" and the sin of both of them is equal.\"" (Tirmidhi) And he said: This hadith is authentic. Its chain is weak"","" said al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5288","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" when Allah intends good for a servant"","" He employs him in (acts of obedience).\"" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! How does He employ him? He said: \""He grants him the ability to do righteous deeds before death.\"" Sahih"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5289","Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The wise person is the one who holds himself accountable and acts for what comes after death"","" and the foolish person is the one who lets his soul follow its desires and places hope upon Allah (that He is Forgiving and Merciful).\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."""""
"5290","It is narrated from a companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: We were sitting in a gathering when suddenly the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived, and there were traces of water (i.e., from bathing) on his head. We said: O Messenger of Allah! We see you in a cheerful mood. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Yes.\"" The narrator states"","" then people began to discuss wealth (whether it is permissible or impermissible). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""There is no harm in wealth for the one who fears Allah"","" and for a pious person"","" good health is better than wealth"","" and true happiness is among the blessings.\"" Its chain is authentic"","" narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5291","Sufyan Thawri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: In the past, wealth was considered undesirable, whereas today it is the shield of a believer. And he said: If we did not have dinars, these kings would consider us worthless. And he said: Whoever has wealth in his hand should make it useful (and not waste it), because this is such a time that if he becomes needy, he will be the first person to sell his religion for worldly gain. And he said: Lawful wealth cannot bear extravagance. Weak, rejected; narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah."
"5292","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \On the Day of Resurrection"","" a caller will call out: Where are those who are sixty years old?\"" And this (sixty years) is the age about which Allah Almighty said: \""Did We not grant you a life long enough for whoever would take heed to take heed"","" and the warner came to you.\"" Its chain of narration is very weak. It was narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5293","Abdullah bin Shaddad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Three men from Banu Udhrah came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they accepted Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Who will take responsibility for their (food and drink) on my behalf?\"" Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I will. So they stayed with him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out an army"","" and one of them went with that army and was martyred. Then he sent out another army"","" and the second man went with it and he too was martyred. Then the third man died on his bed. The narrator says"","" Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I saw all three of them in Paradise (in a dream)"","" and the one who died on his bed was ahead of them"","" the one who was martyred later was with him"","" and the one who was martyred first was with the second (martyr). This confused me"","" so I mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"","" and he said: \""What is strange to you about this? There is no one better in the sight of Allah than a believer who is granted a long life in Islam so that he may glorify"","" magnify"","" and declare the oneness of Allah by saying 'La ilaha illallah'.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5294","Muhammad bin Abi Umairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who was a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), narrated that he said: If a servant were to remain prostrating in obedience to Allah from the day of his birth until he grows old and dies, he would still consider it insignificant on the Day of Resurrection, and he would wish that he could be sent back to the world so that he could increase his reward and recompense. Both narrations have been transmitted by Imam Ahmad. Its chain is authentic, narrated by Ahmad."
"5295","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Seventy thousand individuals from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning; they are those who neither seek ruqyah (spiritual healing)"","" nor take omens"","" and they put their trust in their Lord.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5296","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came and said: \The nations were presented before me. A prophet passed by with one man with him"","" another prophet passed by with two men with him"","" and another prophet passed by with a few men with him"","" while there was a prophet with whom there was not even one person. Then I saw a large group spreading across the horizon. I hoped that this would be my Ummah"","" but I was told that this is Musa (peace be upon him) with his people. Then I was told"","" look"","" and I saw a very large group spreading across the horizon. I was told: Look to this side (right"","" left)"","" and I saw a very large group spreading across the horizon. I was told that this is your Ummah"","" and with them are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. These are the people who neither took bad omens"","" nor sought ruqyah (spiritual healing)"","" nor cauterized"","" and they put their trust only in their Lord.\"" At that moment"","" Ukasha bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said"","" \""Pray to Allah that He makes me among them.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""O Allah! Make him among them.\"" Then another man stood up and said"","" \""Pray to Allah that He makes me among them too.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Ukasha has preceded you in this.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5297","Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The affair of the believer is indeed amazing; all of his affairs are good for him"","" and this is only for the believer. If something good happens to him"","" he is grateful"","" and that is better for him. If something harmful befalls him"","" he is patient"","" and that is better for him.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5298","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than a weak believer"","" though there is good in all (the believers). So strive for that which benefits you"","" seek help from Allah"","" and do not be helpless or lazy. And if any harm befalls you"","" do not say: If I had done (such and such)"","" then (such and such) would have happened; rather say: Allah decreed (this)"","" and whatever He willed"","" He did. For indeed"","" the word 'if' opens the deeds of Satan.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5299","Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \If you put your trust in Allah as He deserves to be trusted"","" He will provide for you as He provides for the birds: they go out hungry in the morning and return full in the evening.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."""""
"5300","Ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O people! I have commanded you regarding everything that brings you closer to Paradise and keeps you away from Hell, and I have forbidden you from everything that brings you closer to Hell and keeps you away from Paradise. Indeed, the Trustworthy Spirit, and in another narration: indeed, the Holy Spirit, has inspired in my heart that no soul will die until it has completed its provision. Listen! Fear Allah and seek provision in a good way, and do not let the delay in provision drive you to seek it through disobedience to Allah, for what is with Allah can only be obtained through His obedience.” Sharh al-Sunnah, al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman, however, Imam al-Bayhaqi did not mention “wa inna Ruh al-Qudus.” Its chain is weak, narrated in Sharh al-Sunnah and al-Bayhaqi in Shu’ab al-Iman."
"5301","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: \Renunciation of the world (zuhd) does not mean making the lawful unlawful and wasting wealth"","" but true renunciation of the world is that what is in your hand is not more trustworthy to you than what is in Allah’s hand"","" and that when you are afflicted with a calamity"","" you do not wish that it had not happened to you"","" hoping for the reward of that calamity.\"" (Tirmidhi"","" Ibn Majah) Imam Tirmidhi said: This hadith is gharib"","" and the narrator Amr bin Waqid is munkar al-hadith. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."""""
"5302","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One day I was (riding) behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: \Boy! Guard (the commands of) Allah"","" Allah will guard you. Take care of (the rights of) Allah"","" you will find Him before you. And when you ask"","" ask only from Allah; when you seek help"","" seek help only from Allah. And know that if the whole nation were to gather together to benefit you with something"","" they would not be able to benefit you except with what Allah has already written for you. And if they were to gather together to harm you"","" they would not be able to harm you except with what Allah has already written for you. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."""""
"5303","Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A person’s good fortune lies in being content with Allah’s decree regarding himself. A person’s misfortune is that he abandons seeking good from Allah, and a person’s misfortune is that he is not content with Allah’s decree regarding himself.” Ahmad, Tirmidhi, and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad and Tirmidhi."
"5304","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he participated in a campaign towards Najd with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, he also returned with him. The Companions were overtaken by sleep (siesta) at noon in a valley full of dense thorny trees. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped there (for rest), and the Companions dispersed in search of the shade of the trees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped under an acacia tree and hung his sword on it, and we slept for a short while. Suddenly, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began calling us. We saw that a Bedouin was with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \He drew my sword against me while I was resting. I woke up and the sword was unsheathed in his hand. He said: 'Who will protect you from me?' I said three times: 'Allah (will protect me).' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not rebuke him for anything and sat down.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5305","And Abu Bakr Isma‘ili narrated in his Sahih as follows: He said, “Who will protect you from me?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “Allah!” The sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took the sword and said, “Who will protect you from me?” He said, “You are the best one to take hold (i.e., forgive),” so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do you bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” He replied, “No, but I promise you that I will not fight you, nor will I support those who fight you.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) let him go (set him free). He (the Bedouin) went back to his companions and said, “I have come to you from the best of people.” It is likewise in Kitab al-Humaydi and Riyadh as-Salihin. Its chain is authentic; it was narrated by an-Nawawi in Riyadh as-Salihin and al-Bayhaqi in Dala’il an-Nubuwwah."
"5306","It is narrated from Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I know of a verse that if people act upon it"","" it will suffice them: 'Whoever fears Allah"","" He will make a way out for him (from every difficulty)"","" and provide for him from where he does not expect.'\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad"","" Ibn Majah"","" and al-Darimi."""""
"5307","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) taught me this verse: \Indeed"","" I alone am the Provider"","" the Possessor of Strength and Power.\"" Abu Dawood"","" Tirmidhi"","" and they said: This hadith is Hasan Sahih. Sahih"","" narrated by Abu Dawood and Tirmidhi."""""
"5308","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), there were two brothers. One of them used to attend the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), while the other used to engage in business. The one who did business complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about his brother. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Perhaps you are provided for because of him.\"" (Tirmidhi) And he said: This hadith is sahih ghareeb. Its chain is hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5309","Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" every valley has a share in the human heart. Whoever lets his heart follow all its shares"","" Allah does not care about him"","" even if He destroys him in any valley. And whoever puts his trust in Allah"","" He suffices him from all shares.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ibn Majah."""""
"5310","It is narrated from Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Your Lord"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has said: If My servants obey Me"","" I will send rain upon them at night and make the sun shine upon them during the day"","" and I will not let them hear the sound of thunder.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5311","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man went to his family, and when he saw their (hunger) need, he went out to the desert (to show humility and helplessness). When his wife saw this, she went to the millstone and set it right, and went to the oven and lit it. Then the woman prayed, \O Allah! Grant us sustenance.\"" She saw that suddenly the tub was filled (with flour). The narrator states: She went to the oven and found it also filled (with bread). The narrator states: When the husband returned"","" he asked"","" \""Did you get anything after me?\"" The wife replied"","" \""Yes! From our Lord.\"" He went to the millstone (to see it). This was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" so he said: \""If he had not lifted (the millstone)"","" it would have kept running until the Day of Resurrection.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5312","Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" sustenance seeks out a servant just as his death seeks him out.\"" Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Abu Nu'aym in Hilyat al-Awliya."""""
"5313","Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It is as if I am seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) describing the incident of a prophet from among the prophets. His people beat him and wounded him, and he was wiping the blood from his face while saying, \O Allah! Forgive my people"","" for they do not know.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5314","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" Allah does not look at your appearances or your wealth"","" but He looks at your hearts and your deeds.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5315","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Allah Almighty says: I am the most independent of all partners from shirk (associating partners with Me); whoever does an action in which he associates someone else with Me"","" I abandon him and his shirk.\"" In another narration: \""I am free from him (the one who does the act); the (act) is for the one for whom he did it.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5316","Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever performs a deed for the sake of fame"","" Allah will disgrace him (before the people) on the Day of Resurrection (because he acted with that intention)"","" and whoever shows off"","" Allah will expose him (to the people) as a show-off.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5317","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), \Tell us"","" a man does a good deed and people praise him for it.\"" In another narration: \""People like him for it.\"" (What is the ruling on this?) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""This is an advance glad tiding for the believer.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5318","Abu Sa’id bin Abi Fadalah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When Allah gathers the people on the Day of Resurrection, about which there is no doubt, an announcer will announce: Whoever associated anyone in a deed which he did for Allah alone, let him seek his reward from someone other than Allah, for Allah is the most free of need of all partners from shirk (associating others with Him).” Hasan, narrated by Ahmad."
"5319","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Whoever shows off his deeds to people"","" Allah will make it heard to His creation"","" and He will humiliate and disgrace him.\"" Sahih"","" narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5320","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever's intention is to seek the Hereafter"","" Allah makes his heart content"","" organizes his affairs"","" and the world comes to him humbled. And whoever's intention is to seek the world"","" Allah places poverty before his eyes"","" scatters his affairs"","" and he gets nothing of the world except what Allah has decreed for him.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5321","Imam Darimi narrated it from Aban’s chain from Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him). Authentic, narrated by Al-Darimi."
"5322","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I said, O Messenger of Allah! While I am in my house on my prayer mat, suddenly a man comes to me and I like the state in which he sees me (is this also showing off?). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Abu Hurairah! May Allah have mercy on you"","" for you there is double reward: the reward for what is hidden and the reward for what is apparent.\"" (Tirmidhi)"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5323","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \In the last era"","" there will appear some people who will seek the world in exchange for religion. They will wear sheep's skins to please the people"","" their tongues (i.e."","" speech) will be sweeter than sugar"","" and their hearts will be like the hearts of wolves. Allah says: They are deceived (thinking that I am giving them respite) or they dare against Me. I swear by Myself that I will send upon such people a trial from among themselves that will leave even their gentle and forbearing ones bewildered.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5324","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: \Allah"","" the Blessed and Exalted"","" said: 'I have created a creation whose tongues are sweeter than sugar and whose hearts are more bitter than aloes. I swear by Myself! I will put them to a trial that will leave even their forbearing (wise and patient) person astonished. Are they deceived because of Me"","" or do they dare against Me?'\"" (Tirmidhi)"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5325","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Indeed"","" everything has a period of enthusiasm and vigor"","" and for every period of enthusiasm and vigor there is also a period of weakness and laziness. If the one who is enthusiastic maintains moderation and avoids excess"","" then hope for his (success)"","" and if fingers are pointed towards him (he becomes famous)"","" then do not count him.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Tirmidhi."""""
"5326","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: \It is sufficient evil for a man that fingers are pointed at him (he becomes notorious) in matters of his religion or worldly affairs"","" except for the one whom Allah protects.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5327","Abu Tamimah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: I was present with Safwan (may Allah have mercy on him) and his companions, and Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) was advising and admonishing them. They asked: Have you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Whoever performs a deed for the sake of fame"","" Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection (showing that he acted with this intention)"","" and whoever puts himself into hardship"","" Allah will put him into hardship on the Day of Resurrection.\"" They said: Advise us. He said: The first thing in a person's body to become corrupt is his stomach"","" so whoever is able to eat only what is lawful should do so"","" and whoever is able to ensure that nothing stands between him and Paradise except a handful of blood which he has unlawfully shed"","" then he must certainly avoid shedding unlawful blood. Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5328","It is narrated from Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that one day he came towards the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he saw Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) crying near the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He asked him: \What is making you cry?\"" He replied: \""What is making me cry is something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Even a small amount of showing off is shirk (associating partners with Allah)"","" and whoever shows enmity to any of my friends has declared war against Allah. Indeed"","" Allah loves those righteous"","" pious"","" and unknown people"","" such that when they are absent"","" they are not missed"","" and when they are present"","" they are not invited"","" nor are they brought close. Their hearts are lamps of guidance"","" and they are kept away from all kinds of turmoil.'\"" (They do not fall prey to any tribulation.) Its chain is weak. It was narrated by Ibn Majah and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5329","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"","" when a servant performs prayer openly"","" he performs it well"","" and when he performs prayer in seclusion"","" he also performs it well. Allah"","" the Exalted"","" says: This is My sincere servant.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ibn Majah."""""
"5330","It is narrated from Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \In the last era"","" there will be some people who will be friends outwardly but enemies inwardly.\"" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! How will this be? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""This will be due to mutual desire (i.e."","" for benefit) and mutual fear (i.e."","" of harm).\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5331","Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Whoever performs prayer to show off has committed shirk; whoever fasts to show off has committed shirk; and whoever gives charity to show off has committed shirk.\"" Both ahadith have been narrated by Imam Ahmad. Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad."""""
"5332","It is narrated from Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) that he began to weep. He was asked, \What is making you weep?\"" He said: \""That which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" when I remembered it"","" it made me weep. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'I fear for my Ummah from shirk and hidden desires.'\"" The narrator states: I said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah! Will your Ummah commit shirk after you?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Yes"","" but they will not worship the sun or the moon"","" nor stones or idols. Rather"","" they will show off their deeds"","" and the hidden desire is that one of them will begin the morning fasting"","" but then a desire from among his desires will come before him"","" so he will break his fast.\"" Weak"","" narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5333","Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us while we were discussing the Messiah Dajjal. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Shall I not tell you about something concerning which I fear for you even more than the Messiah Dajjal?\"" We said: O Messenger of Allah! Please do tell us. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Hidden shirk: it is when a man is performing prayer"","" and when he sees that someone is watching him"","" he lengthens his prayer (making it longer with slow recitation to show off).\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Ibn Majah."""""
"5334","It is narrated from Mahmood bin Labeed (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \What I fear most for you is minor shirk.\"" They asked"","" \""O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by minor shirk?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Showing off (riya).\"" And Imam Bayhaqi has narrated this addition in Shu'ab al-Iman: \""On the Day when Allah will recompense His servants for their deeds"","" He will say to them (those who showed off): Go to those to whom you used to show your deeds in the world"","" and see if you find any reward or goodness with them.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Ahmad and al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5335","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \If a person performs any deed inside a rock that has neither a door nor a window"","" then whatever that deed may be"","" it becomes manifest to the people.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5336","Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If a person has any hidden good or bad trait"","" Allah will manifest a sign from it by which he will be recognized.\"" Its chain of narration is weak. This is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5337","Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \I fear for this Ummah every hypocrite"","" because he speaks with wisdom but acts with oppression.\"" Imam Bayhaqi has narrated all three hadiths in Shu'ab al-Iman. Hasan"","" narrated by al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5338","Muhajir bin Habib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Allah"","" the Exalted"","" says: I do not accept all the speech of the wise"","" but I accept his intention and his purpose. If his intention and purpose are in obedience to Me"","" then I consider his silence as praise and dignity for Myself"","" even if he has not spoken.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by al-Darimi."""""
"5339","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: Abul Qasim, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, said: \By Him in Whose hand is my soul! If you knew (about the punishment of the disobedient) what I know"","" you would weep more and laugh less.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5340","Umm Al-Ala Ansariyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \By Allah! I do not know"","" by Allah! I do not know"","" even though I am the Messenger of Allah"","" what will be done with me and with you?\"" Narrated by Al-Bukhari."""""
"5341","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The fire of Hell was presented before me"","" and I saw in it a woman from the Children of Israel being punished because of a cat. She had tied it up; she neither fed it herself nor let it go so that it could eat the insects of the earth. Thus"","" it died of hunger in that state. And I saw ‘Amr bin ‘Amir Al-Khuzā‘ī dragging his intestines in Hell"","" and he was the first person to introduce the custom of setting animals free in the name of idols.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5342","Narrated from Zainab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her) that one day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me in a state of anxiety, and he was saying: \There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah. Woe to the Arabs because of an evil that has drawn near! Today"","" a hole as big as this has been opened in the barrier of Gog and Magog.\"" And he (peace and blessings be upon him) made a circle with his thumb and index finger. Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I asked"","" \""O Messenger of Allah! Will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Yes"","" when wickedness becomes prevalent.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5343","Abu Amir or Abu Malik Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \There will be people in my Ummah who will consider khaz (a light type of silk) and regular silk"","" wine"","" and musical instruments as lawful. And some people will descend towards the foothills of a mountain"","" and their cattle will go with them. A man will come to them for some need"","" and they will say"","" 'Come back tomorrow.' Allah will punish them during the night and cause the mountain to fall upon them"","" while He will transform the rest of them into monkeys and pigs until the Day of Resurrection.\"" (Bukhari) And in some versions of Mishkat"","" instead of \""khaz\"" it is \""har"",""\"" and this is a scribal error"","" while the correct word is \""khaz.\"" Al-Humaydi and Ibn Athir have considered this version more authentic in this hadith"","" and in the book of Al-Humaydi with the chain of Imam Bukhari"","" and likewise in the commentary of Bukhari by Al-Khattabi"","" it is stated: ((Their cattle will return to them in the evening"","" and a man will come to them for a need...)) Narrated by Bukhari and in Mishkat al-Sunnah."""""
"5344","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When Allah sends punishment upon a people"","" then all the people are encompassed by that punishment. Then"","" on the Day of Resurrection"","" they will be raised according to their deeds.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5345","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Every servant will be resurrected upon the last deed he performed before his death.\"" Narrated by Muslim."""""
"5346","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \I have not seen anything like Hell from which the one fleeing is in such heedlessness"","" nor have I seen anything like the blessings and joy of Paradise for which the one desiring it is in such heedlessness.\"" Sahih"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5347","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \What I see"","" you do not see"","" and what I hear"","" you do not hear. The sky has creaked"","" and it has every right to creak. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! There is not a space of four fingers except that there is an angel placing his forehead in prostration to Allah. By Allah! If you knew what I know"","" you would laugh little and weep much"","" you would abandon enjoyment with women (wives) on your beds"","" and you would go out to the open fields crying out to Allah (in supplication).\"" Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I wish I were a tree that was cut down.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Ahmad"","" al-Tirmidhi"","" and Ibn Majah."""""
"5348","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever fears (danger while traveling at the end of the night) begins his journey in the early part of the night"","" and whoever travels in the early part of the night reaches his destination. Be aware! The merchandise of Allah is precious. Be aware! The merchandise of Allah is Paradise.\"" Weak"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5349","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: \Allah"","" Exalted is His remembrance"","" will say: Remove from the Fire of Hell every person who has remembered Me (with sincerity) even for a single day"","" or who has feared Me at any place.\"" Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and al-Bayhaqi in Kitab al-Ba‘th wa al-Nushur."""""
"5350","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about this verse: \Those who give what they give"","" and their hearts are fearful.\"" I asked"","" \""Are these the people who drink alcohol and steal?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""O daughter of the truthful one! No"","" rather they are those who fast"","" pray"","" and give charity"","" and they fear that it may not be accepted from them. It is they who hasten to good deeds.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah."""""
"5351","Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that when two-thirds of the night had passed, he would stand up and say: \O people! Remember Allah"","" remember Allah"","" the earthquake is about to come"","" immediately after it another earthquake is about to come"","" and death has come with its hardships"","" and death has come with its hardships.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5352","Abu Sa’id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came for prayer and saw the people as if they were laughing. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Listen! If you frequently remembered the destroyer of pleasures (death), it would keep you away from what I have seen (i.e., laughing). So remember often the destroyer of pleasures, that is, death, for the grave says every day: I am the house of strangeness, I am the house of loneliness, I am the house of dust, and I am the house of worms and insects. And when a believing servant is buried, the grave says to him: Welcome! Of all the people who walked upon me, you were the most beloved to me. Today you have been entrusted to me, and you have come to me, so see how I treat you.” He said: “It is expanded for him as far as his sight reaches, and a door to Paradise is opened for him. And when a wicked servant or a disbeliever is buried, the grave says to him: No welcome for you! Of all the people who walked upon me, you were the most hated to me. Today you have been entrusted to me, and you have come to me, so soon you will see how I treat you.” He said: “It becomes constricted for him until his ribs interlock.” The narrator says: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) demonstrated this by interlacing the fingers of one hand into the fingers of the other hand, and said: “Seventy serpents are set upon him, and if one of them were to breathe upon the earth, it would not produce anything as long as the world remains. They will bite and tear at him until he is brought to account.” The narrator says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The grave is either a garden from the gardens of Paradise or a pit from the pits of Hell.” Its chain of narration is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."
"5353","Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The companions said, \O Messenger of Allah! You have grown old.\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""Surah Hud and similar surahs have made me old.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5354","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \O Messenger of Allah! You have grown old.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""Surah Hud"","" Al-Waqi'ah"","" Al-Mursalat"","" 'Amma Yatasa'aloon"","" and Surah Ash-Shams have made me old.\"" (Tirmidhi) And the hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): \""He will not enter Hell.\"" is mentioned in the chapter of Jihad. Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Tirmidhi."""""
"5355","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: You do such deeds which, in your eyes, are finer than a hair (i.e., extremely insignificant), whereas in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we used to consider them destructive. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5356","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Aisha! Avoid even minor sins"","" for there is also a demander (of punishment) from Allah for those sins.\"" Sahih"","" narrated by Ibn Majah"","" Al-Darimi"","" and Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5357","Abu Burdah bin Abu Musa narrates: Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: Do you know what my father said to your father? He said: I do not know. He said: My father said to your father: Abu Musa, does it please you that our Islam in the company of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), our migration in his company, our striving in his company, and all the deeds we did with him remain established and preserved for us, and for the deeds we did after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we remain equal (neither sin nor reward)? At this, your father said to my father: No, by Allah! After the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we strove in jihad, performed prayers, fasted, did many good deeds, and many people accepted Islam at our hands, and we hope for the reward of these deeds. My father said: But I, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), prefer that those deeds (which we did with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) remain established for us, and for all the deeds we did after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we attain equal salvation. I (Abu Burdah) said: Indeed, your father (Umar, may Allah be pleased with him), by Allah! was better than my father. Narrated by al-Bukhari."
"5358","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \My Lord has commanded me with nine things: to fear Allah in secret and in public"","" to speak the truth whether angry or pleased"","" to be moderate in poverty and wealth"","" to maintain relations with those who cut me off"","" to give to those who deprive me"","" to forgive those who wrong me"","" that my silence be for reflection"","" my speech be for remembrance (of Allah)"","" my looking be for taking a lesson"","" and that I enjoin good.\"" I did not find it"","" narrated by Razeen."""""
"5359","Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If tears come out of the eyes of any believing servant out of fear of Allah"","" even if they are as small as the head of a fly"","" and then they flow down his face"","" Allah makes the fire of Hell forbidden for that person.\"" Its chain is weak"","" narrated by Ibn Majah."""""
"5360","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \People (in terms of their conditions and characteristics) are like one hundred camels among which you will hardly find one fit for riding.\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5361","Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \You will surely follow the ways of those before you"","" just as one span matches another span"","" and one cubit matches another cubit"","" so much so that if they entered the hole of a lizard"","" you would follow them in it.\"" It was asked"","" \""O Messenger of Allah! (Are those before us) the Jews and Christians?\"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Who else (could it be)?\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5362","Mirdas Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The righteous people will depart one by one"","" and only useless people will remain"","" like the husk of barley or the refuse of dates"","" who will have no value in the sight of Allah.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhari."""""
"5363","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When my Ummah adopts an arrogant gait and the sons of kings (that is"","" the princes of Persia and Rome) become their servants"","" then Allah will impose the evil ones of this (Ummah) over its good ones.\"" Tirmidhi"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5364","It is narrated from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The Hour will not be established until you kill your caliph"","" fight and kill one another"","" and your evil ones become the inheritors of your world.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5365","Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The Hour will not be established until the most despicable and lowly person will be the one who enjoys the greatest share of the world (its wealth"","" goods"","" and positions).\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi and al-Bayhaqi in Dala'il al-Nubuwwah."""""
"5366","Muhammad bin Ka'b Qurazi narrates: The person who heard from Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me: He said, We were sitting in the mosque with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when suddenly Mus'ab bin Umair (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us. He was wearing only one sheet, which had leather patches on it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw him, he began to weep upon seeing the difference between his previous state of blessings and his current state. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \What will your condition be when one of you will wear one set of clothes in the morning and another in the evening"","" a dish will be placed on your table and another will be removed"","" and you will cover your houses (with curtains and decorations) just as the Ka'bah is covered (with cloths)?\"" The Companions said"","" O Messenger of Allah! At that time we will be better than we are today; we will be free for worship and will be relieved from work (servants will do the work). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""No"","" today you are better than you will be at that time.\"" Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5367","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A time will come upon the people when the one who remains steadfast on his religion will be like one who holds a burning ember in his hand.\"" (Tirmidhi)"","" and he said: The chain of this hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5368","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When your leaders are the best among you"","" your wealthy are generous"","" and your affairs are decided by mutual consultation"","" then the surface of the earth is better for you than its interior (i.e."","" life is better than death). And when your rulers are evil"","" your wealthy are miserly"","" and your affairs are entrusted to women"","" then the interior of the earth is better for you than its surface (i.e."","" death is better than life).\"" (Tirmidhi)"","" and he said: This hadith is gharib. Its chain is weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi."""""
"5369","Thauban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The time is near when (misguided) nations will call each other against you just as eaters call each other to a dish.\"" Someone asked: \""Will it be because we will be few in number on that day?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""No"","" rather on that day you will be many"","" but you will be like the foam of a flood. Allah will remove fear of you from the hearts of your enemies and will cast 'wahn' into your hearts.\"" Someone asked: \""O Messenger of Allah! What is 'wahn'?\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""Love of the world and dislike of death.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Abu Dawood and Al-Bayhaqi in Dala'il al-Nubuwwah."""""
"5370","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When dishonesty becomes widespread among a people, Allah casts fear into their hearts; when adultery spreads among a people, deaths increase among them; when a people cheat in weights and measures, their sustenance is withheld; when a people begin to make unjust decisions, widespread killing occurs among them; and when a people break their covenants, enemies are set over them. Its chain is weak. Narrated by Malik."
"5371","It is narrated from ‘Iyad bin Himar al-Mujashi‘i (may Allah be pleased with him) that one day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his sermon: “Listen! My Lord has commanded me to teach you what He has taught me today, things which you did not know. All wealth that I have bestowed upon any servant is lawful. I have created all My servants as Hunafa (those who keep away from falsehood and are ready to accept the truth). Indeed, the devils come to them and turn them away from their religion, and they make unlawful for them what I had made lawful for them, and they command them to associate with Me that for which I have sent down no authority. Indeed, Allah looked at the people of the earth and detested them, both Arabs and non-Arabs, except for some remnants from the People of the Book. And He said: I have only sent you so that I may test you and test (your people) through you. I have sent down upon you a Book which water cannot wash away (it is unalterable); you will recite it while asleep and awake. Indeed, Allah has commanded me to destroy Quraysh, so I said: My Lord! They will crush my head and make it like bread. He said: Expel them as they expelled you, and fight them, We will support you. Spend, and you will be provided for. Send forth an army, and We will send five armies (of angels) like it. And you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will fight the disobedient with your obedient followers.” Narrated by Muslim."
"5372","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When this verse was revealed: \And warn your closest relatives"",""\"" the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed Mount Safa and began to call out: \""Banu Fihr! Banu Adi!\"" (who are tribes of Quraysh) until they gathered together. Then he said: \""Tell me"","" if I were to inform you that there is an army in the valley intending to attack you"","" would you believe me?\"" They said: \""Yes"","" we have always found you truthful.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""I am a warner to you before a severe punishment.\"" Abu Lahab said: \""May you perish for the rest of the day! Is this why you gathered us?\"" Then the Surah (Tabbat Yada Abi Lahabin Wa Tabb) \""May the hands of Abu Lahab be ruined"","" and ruined is he\"" was revealed. In another narration"","" he called out: \""Banu Abd Manaf! My example and yours is like that of a man who saw the enemy and went to save his family"","" fearing that the enemy would reach them before him"","" so he began to shout loudly: 'Ya Sabahah!'\"" Agreed upon."""""
"5373","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When this verse was revealed: \And warn your nearest relatives"",""\"" the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the Quraysh"","" and they all gathered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed everyone"","" both the general and the specific"","" and said: O Banu Ka'b bin Lu'ayy! Save yourselves from the Fire of Hell. O Banu Murrah bin Ka'b! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Abd Shams! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Abd al-Muttalib! Save yourselves from the Fire. Fatimah! Save yourself from the Fire. I have no power to do anything for you before Allah"","" except that I will uphold the ties of kinship with kindness.And in the narration of Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim"","" the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O assembly of Quraysh! Save your souls (from the Fire by having faith); I can do nothing for you before Allah. O Banu Abd Manaf! I can do nothing for you before Allah. Abbas bin Abd al-Muttalib! I can do nothing for you before Allah. Safiyyah"","" the aunt of the Messenger of Allah! I can do nothing for you before Allah. Fatimah bint Muhammad! Take whatever you wish from my wealth"","" I can do nothing for you before Allah.Narrated by Muslim and al-Bukhari."""""
"5374","Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \This Ummah of mine is an Ummah upon whom mercy has been shown; it will not have (severe) punishment in the Hereafter. Its punishment in this world will be in the form of trials"","" earthquakes"","" and killings.\"" Its chain is Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawood."""""
"5375","Abu Ubaidah and Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: \The beginning of this religion was with prophethood and mercy"","" then there will be caliphate and mercy"","" then there will be oppressive kings"","" then there will be coercion"","" excess"","" and corruption in the land. They will consider silk"","" private parts (adultery)"","" and wine to be lawful. They will be provided sustenance in this state and will continue to be helped until they meet Allah.\"" Its chain is weak; it is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi in Shu'ab al-Iman."""""
"5376","Abu Ubaidah and Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \This religion began with prophethood and mercy"","" then there will be caliphate and mercy"","" then there will be cruel kings"","" then there will be oppression"","" abuse and corruption in the land"","" they will consider silk"","" public places (adultery) and alcohol as halal"","" they will be provided with sustenance on this condition and they will continue to be helped until they meet with Allah.\"" According to the branch of faith."""""
"5377","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Indeed"","" the first thing to be overturned will be...\"" Zaid bin Yahya"","" the narrator"","" said: meaning Islam"","" just as a vessel is overturned"","" meaning wine. It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Allah has already clarified this matter. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: They will change its name and then consider it lawful.\"" Hasan"","" narrated by Al-Darimi."""""
"5378","Nu’man bin Bashir narrates from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Prophethood will remain among you as long as Allah wills, then Allah will remove it when He wills. Then there will be a Caliphate on the pattern of Prophethood for as long as Allah wills, then Allah will remove it when He wills. Then there will be biting kingship for as long as Allah wills, then Allah will remove it when He wills. Then there will be coercive kingship for as long as Allah wills, then Allah will remove it when He wills. Then there will be a Caliphate on the pattern of Prophethood.” Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) fell silent. Habib narrates: When ‘Umar bin ‘Abd al-‘Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) assumed the Caliphate, I wrote this hadith to remind him, and said: I hope that after the oppressive kingship and coercive kingship, you are the Commander of the Faithful. He was pleased with this and liked it. Its chain is authentic. Narrated by Ahmad and al-Bayhaqi in Dala’il al-Nubuwwah."
